{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ju1kzy9o","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":40,"width":260,"height":20},"text":"5  /  DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE · TECHNICAL CONTENT","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/kva183q9","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":72,"width":600,"height":60},"text":"Meridian","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":40,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#17211B","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lwj218ru","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":58,"top":140,"width":600,"height":28},"text":"How I combine content and experience design","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/bqhkvy9s","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":224,"width":180,"height":20},"text":"PROBLEM","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wrq143qx","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":240,"top":221,"width":460,"height":54},"text":"Developers had to move between documentation, authentication, request setup, error handling, and production readiness. The gap between understanding an API and making a successful call created friction.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":15,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#17211B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/xsz2x8ri","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":285,"width":650,"height":0},"geometry":"line","lineColor":"#D9E1D8","lineWidth":1}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/m1ojy98v","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":312,"width":180,"height":20},"text":"DISCOVERY","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nmh0re9g","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":240,"top":309,"width":460,"height":54},"text":"I traced the moments where a developer could lose confidence: finding the right endpoint, knowing what access was required, interpreting a response, recovering from an error, and deciding whether an integration was ready to ship.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":15,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#17211B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/nmd4vqxc","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":373,"width":650,"height":0},"geometry":"line","lineColor":"#D9E1D8","lineWidth":1}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/2l4n2lgr","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":400,"width":180,"height":20},"text":"ACTION","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/pof6xgfi","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":240,"top":397,"width":460,"height":54},"text":"I mapped the journey around developer intent: evaluate, configure access, make the first call, understand the response, recover from failure, and prepare for production. I placed guidance beside execution and wrote the flow so errors explain both the cause and the next action.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":15,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#17211B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/on654byx","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":461,"width":650,"height":0},"geometry":"line","lineColor":"#D9E1D8","lineWidth":1}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/baxozqxo","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":488,"width":180,"height":20},"text":"RESULT","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/apon6lg3","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":240,"top":485,"width":460,"height":54},"text":"The experience connects documentation, runnable requests, response semantics, error recovery, webhooks, and launch readiness in one coherent path. It preserves technical depth while making the next decision easier to find.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":15,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#17211B","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/xcf610fe","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":549,"width":650,"height":0},"geometry":"line","lineColor":"#D9E1D8","lineWidth":1}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/cb658vyt","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":56,"top":576,"width":180,"height":20},"text":"COLLABORATION","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#5D6961","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ret4n6x4","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":240,"top":573,"width":460,"height":54},"text":"I aligned the information architecture with product and engineering constraints around authentication, permissions, request and response behavior, IDs, delivery state, and production controls. I would validate the language with developers and research partners.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":15,"typeface":"Aptos","color":"#17211B","alignment":"left"}}
